Under “word-break: keep-all”, Ladybird now keeps the iteration marks
U+3005, U+303B, U+309D, U+309E, U+30FD, and U+30FE together with the
letters around them, and still breaks after the middle dot and the
ideographic full stop. Run in a box too narrow for any of them, Chrome
157 and WebKit 26.5 did the same on all nine samples. Firefox 151 broke
after each iteration mark, as Ladybird did before. That comparison comes
from running the engines; their code for it wasn’t traced.
